
/* V2.25 · Published rules reference corpus. Read-only; never automatically grants character abilities. */
window.TERRAVALE_V225_FEATS={"beastfolk:environmental-truthsense":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Perception*\n\nYou instinctively read the condition of a place.\n- Increase your **Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you enter a new area, you may ask the DM one of the following:\n  - Is this place **stable, strained, or breaking**?\n  - Is remaining here **safe for prolonged presence**?\n- This sense does not reveal causes or sources.\n\nUsing this feature in rapid succession increases **sensory strain**.","beastfolk:fine-instinct-discrimination":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Perception*\n\nYou have learned to filter instinctive input.\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on checks made to **interpret** instinctual information without panic.\n- You suffer reduced penalties from **low-level sensory strain**.","beastfolk:vibration-pressure-awareness":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Perception*\n\nYou sense subtle disturbances through surfaces and air.\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain advantage on Perception checks to detect:\n  - Structural instability\n  - Approaching movement\n  - Environmental shifts\n- This sense functions even without sight.\n\n---\n# Evasion Traits","beastfolk:instinctive-withdrawal":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Evasion*\n\nYou know when to leave.\n\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When an effect would restrain, grapple, or trap you, you may add your **proficiency bonus** to the escape attempt.\n- Successfully escaping increases sensory strain.","beastfolk:flow-step-repositioning":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Evasion*\n\nYour movement avoids danger rather than confronting it.\n\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Once per turn, when you move at least 10 feet, you do not provoke opportunity attacks from one creature you pass.\n- Using this while overloaded risks instinct bleed-through.\n\n---\n# Endurance Traits","beastfolk:instinctual-grounding":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Endurance*\n\nYou stabilize yourself through physical presence.\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against **exhaustion** caused by environment or magic.\n- You recover from **sensory strain** more quickly in stable areas.","beastfolk:long-exposure-tolerance":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Endurance; Near-Human or Hybrid*\n\nYou endure what others cannot.\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You accumulate sensory strain more slowly in **strained** environments.\n- You may remain functional longer before overload penalties apply.\n\n---\n# Coordination Traits","beastfolk:instinctive-signaling":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Coordination*\n\nYou communicate danger without words.\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Allies within 30 feet gain advantage on their next check to react to environmental danger you have detected.\n- Overuse increases sensory strain.","beastfolk:evacuation-leader":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Coordination*\n\nYou move groups through danger.\n\n- Increase your **Charisma or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Allies who follow your movement ignore the first instance of difficult terrain caused by environment.\n- This ability functions best in short bursts, not sustained retreats.\n\n---\n# Balance & Restraint Traits","beastfolk:instinct-suppression-discipline":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Balance*\n\nYou can quiet instinct when necessary.\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You may delay sensory strain accumulation for a short time.\n- When strain finally applies, it does so **more sharply**.","beastfolk:emotional-regulation":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Balance*\n\nYou maintain composure under pressure.\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **frightened**.\n- While overloaded, you suffer fewer social penalties.\n\n---\n# Attrition Traits","beastfolk:patient-pressure":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Attrition*\n\nYou wear danger down by enduring it.\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain advantage on checks made during **extended challenges** (long travel, sieges, prolonged exposure).\n- This trait does not function during sudden or explosive events.","beastfolk:hold-the-line-instinct":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification with Attrition; Bestial or Hybrid*\n\nYou resist displacement through sheer presence.\n\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on checks and saves against being **moved or knocked prone**.\n- Using this while overloaded risks physical stress.\n\n---\n# Combat Expression Traits (Optional, Feat-Gated)\n\n---","beastfolk:instinctive-natural-weapons":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Animal Classification appropriate to form*\n\nYour body expresses ancient adaptations.\n\n- Increase your **Strength or Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain natural weapons appropriate to your classification.\n- These weapons are extensions of instinct and are **suppressed** during severe overload.\n📌 *This feat is optional and not assumed for Beastfolk.*","beastfolk:predatory-commitment":"*Prerequisite: Beastfolk; Instinctive Natural Weapons*\n\nYou fully commit when conflict is unavoidable.\n\n- Once per turn, when you hit with a natural weapon, you may add your **proficiency bonus** to the damage.\n- Doing so immediately increases sensory strain.\n\n---","crimsonborn:controlled-feeding":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Wisdom or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on Wisdom saves against Feeding Compulsion.\n- When deliberately feeding, you may stop at a lower Feeding Depth than circumstances would otherwise permit.","crimsonborn:blood-savant":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Intelligence or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on checks to assess blood freshness, donor depletion, obvious Pattern Familiarity or broad Aetherion quality.\n- Once per rest, when using Regeneration, you may reduce its Blood State cost by 1, minimum 0, subject to DM balance approval.","crimsonborn:predator-s-patience":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Wisdom or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on Wisdom saves made to resist Blood Thirsty or Feeding Compulsion.\n- While in a Hunger state, you have advantage on appropriate Survival checks to track living prey.","crimsonborn:crimson-physiology":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- Once per feeding interval, when you fail a Constitution Resistance save, reduce the Blood State loss from -8 to -4.\n- Radiant suppression and Aetherion Rejection still function normally.","crimsonborn:bloodbound-dominance":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn, Crimson Stage 2 or higher*\n\n- Increase Charisma or Strength by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- While under Blood Power or Blood Lust, you have advantage on Intimidation checks.\n- When you successfully intimidate a creature while affected by Blood Power or Blood Lust, you may impose disadvantage on that creature's next saving throw against being **frightened or charmed by you** before the end of your next turn.","crimsonborn:hunter-s-instinct":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Dexterity or Wisdom by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- While in Hunger I or worse, you have advantage on Perception and Survival checks directly related to locating fresh blood or living creatures.\n- This does not identify Aetherion compatibility.","crimsonborn:blood-fuelled-recovery":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn, Crimson Stage 2 or higher*\n\n- Increase Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- Once per long rest, after a genuinely nourishing feed, you may remove one non-magical condition the DM agrees could reasonably be purged by accelerated Crimsonborn recovery.\n- If the feed pushes you to +40, resolve Saturation Limit consequences normally.","crimsonborn:ripper-s-wake":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn, DM approval, survived Ripper*\n\n- Increase Strength or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- After recovering from Ripper, you have advantage on the next Wisdom save you make against a Hunger-based compulsion before your next long rest.\n- Narrative and social consequences of known past Ripper events remain intact.","crimsonborn:veiled-predator":"*Prerequisite: Crimsonborn*\n\n- Increase Dexterity or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n- You can conceal ordinary predatory tells more effectively.\n- You have advantage on checks made to pass as non-Crimsonborn when you are not in Hunger III, Critical Hunger, Well-Fed III or Saturation Limit.","daemon:stable-pattern":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou have learned to anchor your form through habit and repetition.\n- Increase your **Constitution or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain advantage on checks made to **maintain a humanoid form** under stress.\n- Minor cosmetic reshaping no longer worsens cohesion loss.\n\n**Notes**  \nThis feat favours social infiltration and long-term disguise.\n\n---","daemon:mutable-anatomy":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou are comfortable reshaping your substance under pressure.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Strength by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You may alter the damage type of your natural weapons freely.\n- Once per short rest, you may form an additional natural appendage (claw, tendril, spike) for one scene. Doing so immediately increases cohesion strain.\n\n---","daemon:ink-blooded-recovery":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYour substance reclaims itself more readily - at a cost.\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you take a short rest, you may partially **reabsorb leaked mass**, reducing cohesion penalties.\n- Using this feature consumes additional power and may trigger instability if overused.\n\n---","daemon:pattern-recognition":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou recognize the structural signatures of mutable beings.\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on checks made to **identify shapeshifters, illusions, or altered forms**.\n- You can sense when a creature is maintaining a form unnaturally, even if you cannot identify how.\n\n---","daemon:fragmented-defense":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou allow your body to partially disperse to avoid harm.\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Once per long rest, when you are hit by an attack, you may reduce the damage taken.\n- Doing so causes visible dispersion and **significant cohesion loss**.\n\n**Notes**  \nThis is survival through instability, not durability.\n\n---","daemon:forced-reformation":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou can violently reclaim your shape when it begins to fail.\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- As an action, you may forcibly stabilize your form.\n- This removes some penalties from cohesion loss, but:\n  - Leaves obvious distortions\n  - Triggers personal failure consequences\n  - Cannot be done repeatedly without escalating risk\n\n---","daemon:split-impulse":"*Prerequisite: Daemon, DM approval*\n\nYou have experimented with dividing your substance.\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You may briefly split part of your mass to perform a simple task (scouting, distraction).\n- Re-joining is costly and dangerous; failure risks permanent instability.\n\n**Notes**  \nThis feat should rarely be used and never casually.\n\n---","daemon:null-tolerant-pattern":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou have adapted - imperfectly - to suppression.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You reduce penalties suffered in **anti-magic or null meridian zones**.\n- You still experience discomfort and suppression - this feat mitigates, not negates.\n\n---","daemon:identity-anchor":"*Prerequisite: Daemon*\n\nYou have cultivated a strong internal sense of self.\n- Increase your **Charisma or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against effects that would:\n  - Override your will\n  - Disrupt your identity\n  - Force unwanted transformation\n- When you fail such a save, the consequences are **personal**, not environmental.\n\n---","daemon:catastrophic-expression":"*Prerequisite: Daemon, DM approval*\n\nYou embrace what happens when restraint fails.\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you suffer severe cohesion loss, you may choose to:\n  - Dramatically alter your form for a short time\n  - Gain significant physical advantage\n- This **guarantees** social exposure and risks environmental fallout.\n\n**Notes**  \nThis feat exists for players who *want* consequences.\n\n---","dvergr:stone-enduring":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYour body is accustomed to long strain beneath weight and pressure.\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against gaining **levels of exhaustion**.\n- When you finish a short rest, you may reduce your current exhaustion level by 1.  \n  Once you use this benefit, you can’t do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\n---","dvergr:heir-of-the-deep-halls":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYou have spent long years navigating ancient tunnels and forgotten places.\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **Perception** or **Survival**.\n- You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks made to detect:\n  - Structural weaknesses\n  - Hidden stone doors\n  - Cave-ins or unstable ground\n\n---","dvergr:unmoving-as-stone":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nOnce you take a stand, it is difficult to make you yield.\n\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You cannot be forcibly moved while you are **conscious** unless you are **incapacitated or restrained**.\n- When a creature attempts to shove you, you may use your **reaction** to gain advantage on the check or saving throw.\n\n---","dvergr:legacy-artisan":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYou have learned not just to craft, but to leave work that lasts.\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Choose one set of artisan’s tools with which you are proficient. You gain **expertise** with those tools.\n- When you craft a non-magical item during downtime, the time required is **halved**, and the item is considered exceptionally durable at the DM’s discretion.\n\n---","dvergr:keeper-of-records":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYou have been entrusted with the memory of stone and oath alike.\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **History** if you don’t already have it.\n- You have advantage on Intelligence (History) checks related to:\n  - Ancient structures\n  - Lineages\n  - Oaths, treaties, and recorded events\n\n---","dvergr:burden-bearer":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYou are accustomed to carrying weight others would abandon.\n\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Your carrying capacity increases by an additional **50%**.\n- You ignore the movement penalties imposed by carrying a heavy load.\n\n---","dvergr:steadfast-survivor":"*Prerequisite: Dvergr*\n\nYou do not fall easily, and you do not fall quietly.\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you are reduced to **half your hit point maximum or less**, you gain advantage on your next **Constitution saving throw**.\n- Once per long rest, when you would be reduced to 0 hit points, you may instead drop to **1 hit point**.\n\n---","elf:long-memory":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYou draw upon centuries of retained knowledge and experience.\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **one skill or tool** of your choice.\n- When you make an ability check using a skill or tool with which you are proficient, you may treat a roll of **7 or lower as an 8**.\n\n---","elf:heightened-awareness":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYour senses are finely tuned to subtle changes in your surroundings.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain advantage on **Perception checks** that rely on sight or hearing.\n- You cannot be **surprised** while you are conscious, unless you are incapacitated.\n\n---","elf:patient-precision":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYou favor careful action over haste.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- If you do not move on your turn, you gain advantage on your **next attack roll or ability check** made before the end of that turn.\n- You may use this benefit a number of times equal to your **proficiency bonus**, regaining all uses after a long rest.\n\n---","elf:refined-discipline":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYou have spent decades mastering a specific practice.\n- Increase one ability score of your choice by **1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Choose one skill or artisan’s tool with which you are proficient. You gain **expertise** with that skill or tool.\n- When you fail an ability check using that proficiency, you may reroll the die and must use the new result.  \n  Once you use this reroll, you can’t do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\n---","elf:trance-adept":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race), Elven Trance trait*\n\nYou have learned to push your meditative state further.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you complete a long rest using **Elven Trance**, you may choose **two** skills or tools to gain temporary proficiency in instead of one.\n- Once per long rest, while in trance, you may remain fully aware of your surroundings.\n\n---","elf:graceful-recovery":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYou recover with controlled efficiency rather than sudden resilience.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you take the **Dodge** action, you gain temporary hit points equal to your **proficiency bonus**.\n- Once per long rest, when you fail a Dexterity saving throw, you may reroll it and must use the new result.\n\n---","elf:worldly-perspective":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYou have lived among many peoples and learned their ways.\n- Increase your **Charisma or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **two additional languages**.\n- You have advantage on **Insight checks** made to assess motives or emotional intent.\n\n---","elf:unhurried-mind":"*Prerequisite: Elf (any elven race)*\n\nYour thoughts remain calm even under pressure.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **confused, frightened, or stunned**.\n- If you succeed on such a saving throw, you may choose to ignore disadvantage on your next ability check before the end of your next turn.\n\n---","kharithen:deepkeeper-s-composure":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Umbrin*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **frightened**.\n- When you succeed on a saving throw against being frightened or charmed, you may gain advantage on your next **Intelligence check** before the end of your next turn.\n\n---","kharithen:preservationist-s-recall":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Umbrin*\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **History** or **Arcana** (your choice).\n- When you make an Intelligence (History) or Intelligence (Arcana) check related to **ruins, ancient works, or lost craft**, you may treat a roll of **7 or lower as an 8**.\n\n---","kharithen:shadowforger-s-hand":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Umbrin*\n\n- Increase your **Strength or Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency with **smith’s tools** or **alchemist’s supplies** (your choice).\n- Once per long rest, when you make an ability check using the chosen tool, you may add **double your proficiency bonus** to the roll.\n\n---","kharithen:ley-depth-sense":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Umbrin*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to detect **hidden doors, hollow spaces, structural weaknesses, or active tunnels** while underground or within stone structures.\n- You cannot be surprised while underground unless you are **incapacitated**.\n\n---\n# Veyl Feats\n*Voices of the Ashlight - Spirit, Memory, Lament*","kharithen:ashlight-vigil":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Veyl*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **Insight** if you don’t already have it.\n- Once per long rest, when a creature you can see within 30 feet fails a saving throw against being **charmed or frightened**, you may use your **reaction** to allow it to reroll the saving throw.\n\n---","kharithen:lament-bearing-presence":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Veyl*\n\n- Increase your **Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on **Persuasion** checks made to calm panic, grief, rage, or escalating conflict.\n- When you succeed on such a check, choose one creature involved; it has disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn.\n\n---","kharithen:keeper-of-gentle-memory":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Veyl*\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **History** or **Medicine** (your choice).\n- When you succeed on a Wisdom (Medicine) check or Intelligence (History) check that relates to a person’s life, death, or identity, you may also learn one additional truthful detail at the DM’s discretion (a name, a bond, a cause, or a missing piece).\n\n---","kharithen:spirit-listening-calm":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Veyl*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **stunned**.\n- Once per long rest, when you fail a saving throw, you may gain a bonus to the roll equal to your **proficiency bonus** (after seeing the roll but before knowing the outcome).\n\n---\n# Thal’ren Feats\n*The Fae-touched - Glamour, Emotion, Balance*","kharithen:glamourweave-mien":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Thal’ren*\n\n- Increase your **Charisma or Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **Deception** or **Performance** (your choice).\n- When you make a Charisma check to influence a creature that can see you, you may add a bonus equal to your **proficiency bonus**. Once you use this bonus, you can’t use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\n---","kharithen:emotion-balancer":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Thal’ren*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **charmed**.\n- When you succeed on a saving throw against charm or fear, choose one creature within 10 feet; it gains advantage on its next saving throw against charm or fear before the end of its next turn.\n\n---","kharithen:boundary-warden":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Thal’ren*\n\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on **Arcana** checks related to planar boundaries, crossings, or fae workings.\n- Once per long rest, when you or an ally within 30 feet would be forcibly moved (shoved, pulled, pushed, or dragged), you may use your reaction to reduce that forced movement by **10 feet**.\n\n---","kharithen:iridescent-shift":"*Prerequisite: Kharithen, Thal’ren*\n\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you take the **Dodge** action, you may also take the **Disengage** action as part of the same action.\n- Once per long rest, when you fail a Dexterity saving throw, you may reroll it and must use the new result.\n\n---","thalassari:tidebound-grace":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Blessed Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you or a willing creature within 10 feet succeeds on a saving throw against being charmed or frightened, choose a different willing creature within 10 feet of you. The chosen creature gains temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus, may move 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks, and has advantage on the next saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn.\n\nYou may grant this blessing a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses when you finish a long rest.\n\n---","thalassari:ocean-s-benediction":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Blessed Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws made against extreme environmental cold and harmful natural deep-water pressure.\n- Once per long rest, when you would gain a level of exhaustion from an environmental cause, you may ignore that level.\n\n---","thalassari:sanctified-breath":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Blessed Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Constitution or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you or a creature you can see within 30 feet begins suffocating or fails a saving throw against an inhaled poison, gas, smoke, or similar airborne or waterborne hazard, you may use your reaction to grant a reroll of that saving throw or suspend the suffocation until the end of the creature's next turn.\n- A creature protected this way also gains temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus.\n\nYou may use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses when you finish a long rest.\n\n---","thalassari:calm-of-the-deep-choir":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Blessed Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Gain proficiency in **Persuasion** or **Performance**. If you already have proficiency in both, gain proficiency in Insight.\n- When you make a Charisma check to calm, guide, or reassure creatures in a stressful or dangerous environment, you may add your proficiency bonus to the roll a second time. Once you use this benefit, you cannot use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\n---\n\n# Adapted Lineage Feats","thalassari:pressure-hardened-physiology":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Adapted Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against exhaustion caused by environmental effects.\n- Difficult terrain caused by water, coral, sediment, or debris costs you no extra movement while swimming.\n- When you are forcibly moved while swimming, reduce that movement by 10 feet. If this reduces the distance to 0, you may remain in your space without falling prone.\n\n---","thalassari:predator-of-the-currents":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Adapted Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made while submerged.\n- Once per turn, when you hit a swimming or submerged creature with an attack roll, add your proficiency bonus to one damage roll of that attack.\n\n---","thalassari:gilled-resilience":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Adapted Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Constitution or Strength by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws and ability checks made to avoid or end the grappled or restrained condition while underwater.\n- When you escape a grapple or restraint underwater, you may immediately move 10 feet without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\n---","thalassari:survivor-s-instinct":"*Prerequisite: Thalassari, Adapted Lineage*\n\n- Increase your **Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Gain proficiency in **Perception** or **Survival**. If you choose a skill in which you are already proficient, double your proficiency bonus for checks using that skill.\n- While submerged or within severe weather, you may take the Search action as a bonus action. When you do, ignore disadvantage on that check caused by rain, spray, suspended sediment, or similar environmental obscurement.\n\nYou may use this bonus action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all uses when you finish a long rest.\n\n---","flugel:aerial-discipline":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYou have trained to fly with restraint rather than bravado.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- While flying, you may **hover until the start of your next turn** (you must still be conscious and unrestrained).\n- Opportunity attacks against you while you are flying are made with **disadvantage**.\n\n---","flugel:wingbound-survivor":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYou know how to function when flight is impossible.\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- If your flying speed is reduced to 0, your **walking speed increases by 5 feet** for the duration.\n- While your wings are impaired, you have advantage on **Athletics** and **Acrobatics** checks made to climb, balance, or reposition.\n\n---","flugel:aether-tuned-resilience":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYour body has learned to stabilize itself amid magical turbulence.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against **wild magic surges**, **planar instability**, and similar magical environmental effects.\n- Once per long rest, when you fail a Constitution saving throw to maintain **concentration**, you may treat it as a success.\n\n---","flugel:controlled-descent":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYou have mastered the art of falling without dying.\n- Increase your **Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You take **no damage** from the first 20 feet of a fall, and half damage from any remaining distance.\n- If you begin falling while conscious, you may move **up to 10 feet horizontally** during the descent.\n\n---","flugel:high-altitude-endurance":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nThin air and biting winds do not slow you.\n- Increase your **Constitution or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You are **acclimated** to high altitude and extreme cold.\n- You have advantage on Constitution saving throws against **environmental exhaustion** caused by altitude, cold, or thin air.\n\n---","flugel:precision-takeoff":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYou launch with efficiency and control.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Strength by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Standing up from **prone** costs you only **5 feet of movement**.\n- Once per turn, when you jump or take off, you may do so **without a running start**.\n\n---","flugel:wingguard-instincts":"*Prerequisite: Flugel*\n\nYou instinctively protect your wings in combat.\n- Increase your **Dexterity or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you take damage while flying, you may use your **reaction** to gain resistance to that damage.\n- Once you use this reaction, you can’t do so again until you finish a **short or long rest**.\n\n---","human:relentless-adaptation":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nYou learn quickly from failure.\n- Increase one ability score of your choice by **1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you fail an ability check, you gain advantage on the **next ability check using the same ability score** before the end of your next turn.\n- You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your **proficiency bonus**, regaining all uses after a long rest.\n\n---","human:jack-of-many-paths":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nYou’ve dabbled in many trades and picked up useful skills along the way.\n- Increase one ability score of your choice by **1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Gain proficiency in **two skills** of your choice.\n- Whenever you make an ability check with a skill you are **not proficient in**, you may add **half your proficiency bonus** (rounded down) to the roll.\n\n---","human:stubborn-resolve":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nYou refuse to give up, even when others would falter.\n- Increase your **Constitution or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **frightened**.\n- When you fail a saving throw against being frightened or charmed, you may reroll the save and must use the new result.  \n  Once you use this reroll, you can’t do so again until you finish a long rest.\n\n---","human:opportunistic-thinker":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nYou excel at spotting openings and making the most of imperfect situations.\n- Increase your **Intelligence or Dexterity by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you roll initiative, you may immediately take one of the following:\n  - Draw or stow an item\n  - Move up to **10 feet**\n  - Make a **Perception or Investigation** check\n- You can do this once per combat.\n\n---","human:natural-leader":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nOthers look to you when decisions must be made.\n- Increase your **Charisma or Wisdom by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **Persuasion** or **Intimidation**.\n- As a bonus action, you can choose one ally within **30 feet** who can see or hear you.  \n  That ally gains advantage on their **next ability check or saving throw** before the end of their next turn.  \n  Once you use this ability, you can’t use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\n---","human:learned-versatility":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nYou have formal training across a wide range of disciplines.\n- Increase your **Intelligence by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- Gain proficiency with **two tools, vehicles, or gaming sets** of your choice.\n- Once per long rest, when you make an ability check using a tool with which you are proficient, you may treat the roll as if you had rolled a **10** on the die.\n\n---","human:against-the-odds":"*Prerequisite: Human*\n\nWhen everything goes wrong, you find a way to endure.\n- Increase one ability score of your choice by **1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you are reduced to **half your hit point maximum or less**, you gain advantage on your next **saving throw**.\n- Once per long rest, when you would be reduced to 0 hit points, you may instead drop to **1 hit point**.\n\n---","oni:trial-hardened":"*Prerequisite: Oni*\nYou have endured repeated trials meant to break the unworthy.\n- Increase your **Constitution or Strength by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you make a saving throw against **exhaustion**, you have advantage on the roll.\n- When you succeed on a saving throw that would impose the **frightened** condition, you can choose to ignore the source of that effect until the end of your next turn.\n\n---","oni:iron-will-under-pressure":"*Prerequisite: Oni*\nYour mind does not bend easily when challenged.\n- Increase your **Wisdom or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You have advantage on saving throws against being **charmed**.\n- If you are charmed and the effect allows a saving throw at the end of each turn, you may immediately repeat the saving throw once when the effect is first applied.\n\n---","oni:unbreakable-stance":"*Prerequisite: Oni*\nYou have mastered the art of standing firm, no matter the force against you.\n- Increase your **Strength or Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You cannot be knocked **prone** while you are conscious unless you are **restrained or incapacitated**.\n- When a creature attempts to shove you, you may use your **reaction** to impose disadvantage on the attempt.\n\n---","oni:scarred-but-standing":"*Prerequisite: Oni*\nYour scars are lessons, not weaknesses.\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- When you are reduced to **half your hit point maximum or less**, you gain advantage on your next **saving throw or Constitution check**.\n- Once per long rest, when you take damage that would reduce you to 0 hit points, you can reduce the damage so that you are instead reduced to **1 hit point**.\n\n---","oni:dominant-presence":"*Prerequisite: Oni*\nYour presence alone is enough to make others hesitate.\n- Increase your **Strength or Charisma by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- You gain proficiency in **Intimidation**. If you already have it, you gain expertise in Intimidation instead.\n- As a bonus action, you may attempt to **intimidate one creature** that can see and hear you within 10 feet.  \n  The creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Charisma modifier) or have disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn.  \n  Once you use this ability, you can’t use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\n---","oni:rite-of-endurance":"*Prerequisite: Oni, 8th level*\nYou have completed a formal trial recognized by Oni tradition.\n- Increase your **Constitution by 1**, to a maximum of 20.\n- At the start of each of your turns while you are **grappled, restrained, frightened, or poisoned**, you gain temporary hit points equal to your proficiency bonus.\n- If you are affected by multiple of these conditions simultaneously, this feature still triggers only once per turn.\n\n---"};
window.TERRAVALE_V225_SUBCLASSES={"echo-bearer":{"Discipline of the Remembered Blade":"Level 3 — Martial Continuity. Permanently gain medium armour, shield and martial weapon proficiency , independent of active Aspect. Select one Fighting Style (no duplicate selections): Style Benefit Archery +2 to attack rolls with ranged weapons. Defence +1 AC while wearing armour. Dueling +2 damage using one-handed melee weapon with no other weapon; shield allowed. Great Weapon Fighting With a two-handed Two-Handed/Versatile melee weapon , reroll damage dice showing 1 or 2 , use new roll. Two-Weapon Fighting Add ability modifier to damage of extra Light weapon attack, including if Nick moves it into Attack action. Level 3 — Remembered Weapon. After each long rest , choose one proficient wea","Discipline of the Living Chorus":"Level 3 — Chorus Companions. After each long rest , choose Wis modifier (minimum 1) willing creatures with whom you spent ≥10 minutes resting, talking, travelling or training during preceding day . They remain Companions until next long rest. You always count as your own Companion , without using a slot. Level 3 — Shared Cadence. Reaction when Companion within 30 ft that can see/hear you makes attack/check/save: expend Echo Die and add to roll after d20/before result. Whenever you switch active Aspect , one Companion within 30 ft can gain its selected skill/tool aptitude until Aspect ends, you reassign it, or Companion stays over 60 ft away for 1 minute . Blade: instead martial weapon you ca","Discipline of the Gentle Unburdening":"Level 3 — Practitioner of Unburdening. Gain Medicine and one of: calligrapher's supplies, herbalism kit, or musical instrument. If already proficient in one of these proficiencies, double proficiency bonus on checks with it instead . Level 3 — Quiet the Intrusion. Reaction when another creature within 30 ft fails Int/Wis/Cha save : expend Echo Die and add it, potentially succeeding. If still failed and effect immediately deals psychic damage , reduce that damage by die + Wis . Level 3 — Unburdening Touch. Action; touch willing creature: expend die; restore die + Wis HP ; creature may repeat a save against one charm/fear effect , adding same die to save. Each target can heal from this only on"},"scarlet masque":{"Veiled Courtier":"3rd — Institutional Cover. During preparation, give one constructed Masque cover in a studied court, guild, temple, clinic, army, household, trading organisation, etc. While active: advantage on Int checks to remember public procedures/ranks/uniforms/duties; First Impression can instead benefit Int (History), Int (Investigation) or Wis (Insight) for navigating institution. Minor missing appointment, insignia or paperwork prompts verification, not instant exposure. No real documents, secret knowledge or legal authority. 3rd — Expected Entourage. When adopting constructed Masque, choose ≤Cha modifier willing creatures within 30 ft ; for 1 hour (or until used again), they can pass as plausible ","Red Witness":"3rd — Blood Evidence. 1-minute examination of fresh bloodstain/sample/wound; learn three evidence-supported facts: alive when shed, apparent creature type, physiological strain/poison/disease/starvation/overfeeding, match to observed creature, same source as another sample, close hereditary relation, alchemical/Hematurgic/transformation contamination, physical emotion/consciousness when shed, or sample's approximate age. No name, memories, exact place, guilt or full narrative. PB uses/long rest ; suitable lab/kit can group related samples into a single investigation. 3rd — Witness’s Regard. Upon Regard, mark one current target as subject of inquiry until Regard ends (one subject normally). Y","Velvet Knife":"3rd — Concealed Practice. Gain poisoner's kit or thieves' tools proficiency (if both, choose a Scarlet Masque skill instead). Draw/stow one-handed weapon as part of each attack with it. Detection checks for properly concealed Tiny weapon/dagger have disadvantage unless physically searched. Prepared playing card, hairpin, fan rib, surgical implement etc. functions as a dagger dealing piercing/slashing (choose when prepared). 3rd — Knife in the Applause. On your own finesse, ranged or concealed weapon attack when you apply Needle Opening , add 1d4 weapon-type damage ( 1d6 at 11 , 1d8 at 17 ). Nonlethal with qualifying melee weapon per ordinary rules. 6th — Redirect the Eye. Reaction + 1 Thread"},"chaos arsenal":{},"gatewarden":{"Iron Threshold":"Level 3 — Standing Interposition. Reaction: When an authorised creature within 5 ft of you or your Gate is targeted by an attack, move up to 5 ft (no opportunity attack from attacker) and become its target. End within 5 ft of protected creature; attack must be able to target you. Original attack roll is tested against your AC . After resolution, optionally spend a Fortification Die to reduce damage you take by die + Con modifier . Level 3 — Hold Their Attention. On Gate Response hit, target has disadvantage attacking anyone other than you until start of your next turn. Ends early if you become incapacitated or target moves more than 30 ft away. Level 7 — No Further. While Braced, Gate Respon","Bridgekeeper":"Level 3 — Safe Crossing. Once on each authorised creature's turn, if it begins movement within 5 ft of Gate , it can move 5 ft without opportunity attacks or spending its remaining speed. Cannot stack with Formation Discipline's added movement: from level 9, use either to move 10 ft instead. Level 3 — Shared Footing. When using Anchor the Line, Brace the Blow, Close the Line, or Measured Retreat to protect an authorised creature, roll the expended die twice , use either result. Level 7 — Carry the Formation. Once per own turn when you move, one willing authorised creature within 5 ft of you may spend its reaction to follow you up to your movement distance. No opportunity attacks; must stay w","Collapse Engineer":"Level 3 — Field Constructor. Gain mason's or carpenter's tools proficiency; if already proficient, double PB with them. Gain Hasty Barricade at level 3. At level 6, its cover improves to three-quarters for creatures directly behind it, its AC becomes 17 , and its HP increase by 2 × Gatewarden level . Level 3 — Measured Ruin. Once per turn , weapon hit against an object or construct deals +PB damage . Weapon attacks against objects/structures ignore resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning/piercing/slashing, ignore damage threshold up to PB , and deal full damage even with an otherwise unsuitable weapon if you identify a structural weakness. Level 7 — Controlled Collapse. Action; one die: collaps"},"ventweaver":{"Storm-Choral":"Level 3 — Shared Tempo: Once/round when you gain Flow on your turn, a willing creature you see within 30 ft may use reaction to move 10 ft , no opportunity attacks. If moving through your Sustained Pattern, no reaction needed but movement becomes 5 ft . This can contribute to your normal outside-turn Flow trigger only once. Level 3 — Choral Pressure: Gain musical instrument proficiency (if already proficient, another instrument/tool). Pressure Lance/Pattern force damage may become thunder . Once on each of your turns , when a Pattern moves 2+ creatures , one moved hostile creature or unattended object takes thunder damage equal to your Wisdom modifier (willing ally only with consent). Level ","Descent Warden":"Level 3 — Catch the Descent: Reaction; visible creature within 60 ft , when falling/forcibly moved. Choose Break the Fall: reduce falling distance for damage by 10 ft × Ventweaver level , then optionally move 10 ft horizontally to a no-more-dangerous route; or Check the Movement: reduce forced movement by 10 ft , and if reduced to 0, move creature 5 ft to empty legal space. Optional 1 Flow : Break the Fall makes all falling damage 0 , or Check reduces movement by another 10 ft . Protecting another qualifies for outside-turn Flow after resolution. Level 3 — Guided Passage: Willing creatures moved by your Ventweaver features provoke no opportunity attacks. When your Pattern moves another creat","Ruin Mediator":"Level 3 — Structural Listener: Proficiency Arcana or Investigation (if already proficient, double PB on checks with chosen skill to inspect magical structures/wards/constructs/ruins/hazards). Pressure Sense yields two facts . Once/turn when a magical hazard, ward, construct or lingering spell within Pressure Sense range activates/changes, mark Observed Instability until end of your next turn; first Pattern directly affecting/protecting against/moving it costs 1 less Flow , minimum 1 . Level 3 — Damp the Backlash: Reaction + 1 Flow to reduce damage to visible creature within 30 ft from spell/magical hazard/unstable construct/ward by 1d8 + Wisdom modifier , increasing to 2d8 + Wisdom modifier "},"shaman":{"The Vessel":"3 — Open Vessel: Bonus Action deepen channel 1 min, PB uses/recovery . Numerical Presence improves by PB or one Favour die as appropriate ; nonnumerical gets advantage on directly supported checks. Once/turn after Invocation gain temp HP = Wis . 6 — Shared Flesh: while Deepened choose one approved trait: climb/swim/fly during turn; +1 AC ; darkvision/blindsight 10 ft ; elemental resistance; natural weapon using Favour die . 10 — Safe Possession: Embodiment costs 1 fewer die, min 1 ; advantage vs involuntary possession/identity alteration; once/Embodiment turn one failed such save into success. 14 — Two Voices, One Body: during Embodiment keep second Bond's Presence; once/turn after embodied ","The Warden":"3 — Warding Sigils: learn Threshold Ward and Anchor Ward in addition to normal Rites. Anchor Ward: Action, creature within 30 ft gains advantage vs possession/forced teleport until next turn. Either Ward used in combat costs 1 Favour die . 6 — Exorcist's Rebuke: Reaction when a spirit, possessor, curse-manifestation, summoned or incorporeal entity within 30 ft uses a supernatural feature. Spend/roll 1 Favour die to subtract from its attack/save-DC outcome or deal 2× die result force/spirit damage. If subtraction causes failure, push the manifestation 10 ft . 10 — Circle of Refusal: Action + 2 Favour , 15-ft aura, 1 min . Hostile spirits/summons entering/starting: Wis save; fail = Speed 0 and","The Ancestor Keeper":"3 — Keeper of Names: History or Religion proficiency (expertise if already proficient). 10-min rite at grave/relic/community record: ask one question of residual ancestral memory if soul law permits; no soul summoning. Ancestral Counsel: PB times/recovery , add Favour die after an ally's skill/save roll when memory, duty, lineage, craft or survival is relevant. 6 — Inherited Skill: after recovery, choose one justified ancestral/community/taught skill, tool or weapon tradition; gain proficiency, or expertise if already proficient in the skill. Change after a meaningful ancestral rite. 10 — Stand Behind Me: Reaction, ally 30 ft takes damage → 1 Favour reduces by die + Wis + half Shaman level ;","The Spiritwalker":"3 — Between-Step: Bonus Action + 1 Favour teleport 5 × die result ft to visible space; instead pass through one occupied square/ 5 ft non-warded solid material and emerge adjacent. No Null/Seals. 6 — Far Hearing: while Channeling, sense bonded spirits/major spirit activity within 1 mile on the same local spiritual layer. 10-min rite: project senses to a known spirit-path location within 1 mile for up to 10 min ; body is unaware of its surroundings. 10 — Escort the Living: Spirit Crossing may bring up to PB willing creatures touching you ; each uses its Reaction and arrives adjacent. Spiritual-layer stay lasts at most 10 min ; party returns together unless local rules permit otherwise. 14 — P","The Wild Speaker":"Ordinary natural/local spirits and ecologies , not true Primals by default. 3 — Local Kinship: Nature/Survival proficiency/expertise; communicate simple ideas with Beasts, aware plants and ordinary nature spirits. After 10 min in a new natural region, learn one truthful environmental fact. 6 — Borrowed Adaptation: while Channeling choose climb Speed; swim + water breathing; darkvision 60 ft ; +10 Speed ; or one supported environmental damage resistance. 1 Favour gives it to ally for 10 min . 10 — Land Answers: Action + 2 Favour , 20-ft area, 1 min . Enemy difficult terrain; allies ignore natural difficult terrain + gain half cover from natural features. Once/turn move one ally 10 ft via envi"},"summoner":{"Conduit":"3 — Stable Projection. Early limited Projection: Bonus Action , 1 min , initially adjacent; AC 13+PB , HP 3×level+Cha , Speed 30 , max distance 30 ft ; attack uses your Eidolon attack bonus and Manifestation die+Cha damage. One safe use/recovery , later uses +1 Strain. At Lv5, switches to regular Projection stats/HP. 6 — Long Leash. Projection range 120 ft ; Bonus Action perceive through it until next turn. It acts through your action economy , never an extra full turn. 10 — Dual Presence. Use Partial forms personally while Projected. Once/turn , if both you and Eidolon affect same target, deal +1 Manifestation die damage or grant ally Manifestation die+Cha temp HP . 14 — Independent Will. O","Vessel":"3 — Early Merge. Bonus Action, 1 min , one safe use/recovery, later +1 Strain. Choose two Concept-supported traits : +1 AC; +10 ft Speed; climb/swim; +5 ft reach; darkvision or blindsight 10 ft; natural weapon (Manifestation die); or thematic damage resistance until start next turn after spending a Technique . 6 — Shared Anatomy. Early Merge adds third trait ; activation temp HP level+Cha . On Price escalation, reduce first numerical penalty/damage by PB ; narrative Price remains. 10 — Dominant Form. During Merged, choose one Major Trait each merge : fly Speed equal to Speed; Large if space permits; one damage resistance; extra Reaction for Contract defence only; or once/turn +1 Manifestatio","Shaper":"3 — Many Forms. Learn two extra Partial forms , maintain two simultaneously . Concept-appropriate examples: martial-profile weapon (Cha), shield +1 AC , armour temp HP =level , grapple/reach limb, darkvision eye, +10 Speed/climb movement organ, artisan/thieves' tool. 6 — Adaptive Shaping. Bonus Action reshape one active Partial form. Once/turn after reshaping, move 10 ft without provoking or gain +PB to next attack/check using new form. 10 — Complex Manifest. Maintain three Partial forms; one may be Complex: two-handed/area weapon; armour +2 AC, −5 ft Speed ; wings (fly during turn); extended limbs +10 ft reach ; sensory crown blindsight 20 ft . Initial Complex manifest +1 Strain , unless us","Ascendant":"3 — Court the Price. Safe Strain +1 . On deliberately crossing Safe Strain, choose Surge until next turn: +PB AC ; +10 ft Speed and no opportunity attacks; +1 Manifestation die damage once; or advantage on all saves . Price still escalates. 6 — Controlled Overreach. Once/recovery , gain 2 Strain instead of 1 to take an extra Bonus Action for Manifestation/Technique or reroll a failed Technique attack/save interaction. Cannot chain extra actions/spells. 10 — Evolving Under Pressure. First time/recovery you reach maximum Safe Strain , gain compatible temporary Evolution until Strain resets: flight, +1 AC , +10 Speed , extra Technique known, resistance or enlarged Projection. 14 — Break Without"},"shadowforger":{"Black Edge":"Level 3 — Flowing Arsenal. Once on each of your turns , Reforge an Armament without an action immediately before its attack (normal Temper loss applies until level 9). Each form gains: Edge — Exact Cut: Once/turn while attacking with advantage, reroll one attack damage die . Breaker — Driving Blow: Once/turn on hit, push target 5 ft if at most one size larger than you. Reach — Catch the Step: Opportunity attacks also trigger when a creature enters reach; same creature at most once during its turn. Volley — Unobstructed Line: Ignore half cover ; hostile creature within 5 ft does not impose ranged disadvantage. Twin — Paired Intent: Add your ability modifier to the additional attack from Terra","Sepulchral Mantle":"Level 3 — Living Mantle. While Aegis active, Turn the Blow range 10 ft . Protecting someone else reduces PB + INT modifier (your own reduction still PB), and lets you move 5 ft toward them as part of reaction without provoking from damage source. If Aegis active and no separate Armament, manifest a one-handed Mantle Blade within same Forging ( 1d6 bludgeoning/piercing/slashing, Finesse); counts as Armament for attacks/techniques, but has no separate Temper or Killing Fracture. Level 7 — Stored Violence. When your Aegis gains Temper from a visible creature's damage, mark it until end of your next turn ; first Armament hit on it deals + one Gloam Die force (free). Add Returned Weight Aegis Sha","Hollow Architect":"Level 3 — Second Foundation. Maintain one extra Structure-only Forging beyond normal limit (own Temper; Reforge only into Structure). Increased Structure max size: Large/4 sections at level 3 , Huge/9 at level 6 , Gargantuan/16 at level 13 (never bigger; coherent shape). Each Structure section gains INT modifier + PB maximum HP. Use INT on artisan's tool checks for physical construction/design/inspection/dismantling/repair. Level 7 — Designed Terrain. On creation/Reforge of a Structure choose one purpose until next Reforge: Bastion: each section gains temporary HP = Shadowforger level . Passage: selected creatures ignore difficult terrain created by/immediately beside it; first 10 ft of movi"},"pressurebearer":{"Unmoving Line":"3 — Claim the Line. Bonus action, 1 Pressure , claim moving 10-ft radius for 1 minute ; ends on incapacitation or if you willingly move more than half speed in a turn . Hostiles treat area as difficult terrain. Reaction when hostile in your reach attacks another creature: melee attack counting as an opportunity attack ; first opportunity-attack hit each round grants 1 Pressure . Driving: extend claimed area along your movement path that turn. Bearing: allies inside advantage vs forced movement. Anchoring: radius +5 ft . 6 — No Passage. Opportunity-attack hit reduces target speed to 0 for rest of turn . Once/round when hostile enters your reach, move 5 ft toward it without reaction . 10 — Liv","Shared Burden":"3 — Burden Bonds. After long rest bond PB willing creatures until next long rest. Reaction when bonded creature within 30 ft takes damage: reduce by PB + CON ; you suffer equal unreducible force damage , and generate 1 Pressure . In Bearing, combine with Bear the Blow; take self-damage only from Bear the Blow's calculation . Apply universal one-hop damage routing . 6 — Hand It to Me. Reaction, 2 Pressure when bonded creature within 30 ft fails save vs Charmed, Frightened, Poisoned, Restrained, Dazed, or Stunned : ally ignores condition until end of your next turn ; you suffer it instead. At that turn's end ally repeats save: success ends, failure restores it unless otherwise removed. Restrai","Breaking Point":"3 — Aggressive Compression. Once/turn , trigger Driving Pressure regardless of stance. If already Driving, your first committed strike each turn deals +CON damage while Redlined . 6 — Directed Rupture. Your Ruptures/Breaks do not push, prone, or create difficult terrain for designated allies . Hostiles failing save vs your Driving Rupture/Break also take force damage = Pressurebearer level . On Bearing or Anchoring Rupture , optionally create 15-ft force cone : creatures STR save or take 2d8 force and get pushed 10 ft . 10 — Violent Economy. Once/turn , offensive Release spending 2+ Pressure that hits or forces failed save restores 1 Pressure after resolution , counts towards 3/round gain ca","Long Watch":"3 — Read the Unstable. Gain Arcana or Investigation proficiency (if already proficient, double PB for chosen skill). Use Read the Load as bonus action PB times/long rest . On successful in-combat read of a creature, additionally learn one: weakest STR/DEX/CON save; whether concentrating; whether sustained by outside magical effect; or whether close to losing control of condition, transformation, or magical state. 6 — Delay the Burden. Reaction, 2 Pressure when creature within 30 ft suffers magical damage/fails save against magical effect: defer its damage/condition until end of your next turn . Before then spend additional Pressure to reduce delayed damage 1d8 per Pressure , transfer to your"},"seal-maintainer":{"Silent Seal":"1 — Suppression Script: Suppress (always prepared). Brand/Anchor; choose one: teleportation, transformation, regeneration, invisibility, summoning, possession, magical flight, initiation/sustaining repeated steps of an effect, or one observed supernatural action. Attempt Breaches; appropriate save/ability check vs Seal DC. Failure stops process but spends action/resource; success works; both remove 1 Integrity . Spell level exceeding PB, legendary/comparably strong action may cost +1 Integrity (DM). Other subjects require study/DM consent. 1 — Read the Disturbance. Bonus action after witnessing supernatural effect within 60 ft ; learn two : internal/external source, need for concentration/up","Closed Road":"1 — Threshold Script: No Further (always prepared). Anchor modifying Do Not Cross: choose entry, exit, crossing line, approaching protected subject, transporting named object out, or advancing past point. Normal Do Not Cross effect; Breach also lowers creature speed by 10 ft until end turn. 1 — Answer the Crossing. Reaction on hostile creature entering/crossing/Breaching Threshold: move up to half speed toward talisman or trigger; no opportunity attack from trigger. 6 — The Road Is Watched. One Threshold capacity-free . Answer the Crossing now moves up to full speed and makes sealed-weapon attack on trigger; on hit normal weapon damage plus choose: end remaining movement, or Strength save to","Burden-House":"1 — Sanctuary Script: Take Shelter (always prepared). Ward/Anchor protecting designated creatures in Ward/area. Once/round , reaction on protected creature taking damage: reduce by Wisdom modifier + PB ; Sanctuary loses 1 Integrity . 1 — Hands of the House. Whenever you repair Sanctuary Integrity, heal one protected creature for one Inscribed Strike die roll + Wisdom modifier (before level 2: 1d6 + Wisdom modifier ). PB uses/long rest ; extra healing costs one spent Hit Die (no self-healing roll). Same creature benefits at most once/round . 6 — The Door Remains Open. One Sanctuary capacity-free . Reaction on damage to protected creature in Maintenance Range, choose one, not multiple: Absorb:","Severing Script":"1 — Opening Script: Expose (always prepared). Hostile Brand via sealed-weapon hit or seal attack. First Breach by target each round grants 1 Severing Mark , max 2 , lost when Brand ends. The applying hit cannot benefit from already-active-Brand effects. 1 — Cut Along the Line. Once/turn , hit on Opening Brand target deals +1d6 weapon-type damage , stacks with Inscribed Strike. 6 — The Opening Widens. One Opening Brand capacity-free , max 3 Marks . On application learn one target resistance/immunity; existence of regeneration; main AC source (armour/natural/speed/magic); or a reinforcing effect. Your talisman weapon treats resistance to its damage as none, immunity as resistance. 10 — Rupture"},"oracle of the two waters":{"Choir of the Silver Current":"Bonus spells Oracle level Always prepared (Tyrian) 3 healing word, sanctuary, aid, lesser restoration 5 aura of vitality, mass healing word 7 aura of life, freedom of movement 9 greater restoration, mass cure wounds 3rd — Current of Mercy. Once per turn , when an Oracle spell or Tyrian Petition heals a creature or reduces damage to it, that creature may: move 5 ft without opportunity attacks; gain temp HP = PB ; or end Grappled if grappler is at most one size larger. You may benefit yourself. Ending grapple does not automatically end independent Restrained/Pinned effects. 6th — Breath Shared, Burden Divided. Once per turn , when a levelled Oracle spell or Tyrian Petition heals only one creat","Choir of Stillwater":"Bonus spells Oracle level Always prepared (Kalman) 3 bane, false life, gentle repose, silence 5 revivify, speak with dead 7 death ward, divination 9 antilife shell, hallow 3rd — Keeper at the Threshold. Always know when a seen creature 60 ft is at 0 HP or died in past 1 minute . As bonus action , pick one creature at 0 HP within 60 ft : Hold: Stabilise it. Hear: While unconscious, it hears/understands speech until end of your next turn and communicates one telepathic emotion/image/sentence to you. Release: A willing creature—or non-player creature whose death DM accepts—dies peacefully, protected from soul-capture/consumption/undeath for 24 hours . Never kills an unwilling conscious creature","Choir of Warning":"Bonus spells Oracle level Always prepared (Confluence) 3 detect magic, feather fall, augury, see invisibility 5 clairvoyance, counterspell 7 arcane eye, divination 9 legend lore, scrying 3rd — Pressure Signs. Add Wis modifier to initiative. While conscious ignore initiative disadvantage caused by Surprise. Prepare one extra Omen ; Held-Omen capacity unaffected. 6th — Warning Before Impact. Reaction , seen creature 60 ft makes attack/check/save; after d20 but before outcome spend 1 Answer Die to add/subtract it. PB uses/long rest , each still costs a die. Counts as Confluence use, not a Tyrian/Kalman Petition. 10th — Repeated Pattern. After long rest designate one prepared Omen; it can be ful","Choir of the Abyssal Confluence":"Bonus spells Oracle level Always prepared (Confluence) 3 armour of Agathys, thunderwave, darkvision, shatter 5 tidal wave, water breathing 7 control water, watery sphere 9 maelstrom, telekinesis 3rd — Tideglass Conduit. Stress maximum rises to 7 ; at 6 remain under Stress 5's penalties , and choose Shatter/Take the Mark only at 7 . When gaining ≥1 Stress, receive temp HP = Oracle level ( once per turn ). 6th — Shape the Pressure. Bonus action , spend 1 Answer Die to create a 15-ft-radius field centred at a point seen within 60 ft , lasting 1 minute with concentration (as a spell). Pick Dense or Buoyant ; swap as bonus action on later turns. Dense: Hostile creatures treat area as difficult te"}};

window.TERRAVALE_V225_MD=function(raw){
 const E=s=>String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
 const I=s=>E(s).replace(/\*\*([^*\n]+)\*\*/g,'<strong>$1</strong>').replace(/(?<!\*)\*([^*\n]+)\*(?!\*)/g,'<em>$1</em>').replace(/`([^`\n]+)`/g,'<code>$1</code>');
 // Some imported feat excerpts include the heading of the following feat group. This is a boundary artefact.
 let body=String(raw||'').replace(/\r\n?/g,'\n').replace(/\n---\s*\n#\s+[^\n]+\s*$/,'').replace(/\n---\s*$/,'').trim();
 let lines=body.split('\n'), result=[], list=false, para=[];
 const closePara=()=>{if(para.length){result.push('<p>'+I(para.join(' '))+'</p>');para=[]}};
 const closeList=()=>{if(list){result.push('</ul>');list=false}};
 for(const original of lines){const line=original.trim();
  if(!line){closePara();continue}
  if(/^---+$/.test(line)){closePara();closeList();continue}
  if(/^#{1,5}\s+/.test(line)){closePara();closeList();result.push('<h4>'+I(line.replace(/^#{1,5}\s+/,''))+'</h4>');continue}
  if(/^[-*]\s+/.test(line)){closePara();if(!list){result.push('<ul>');list=true}result.push('<li>'+I(line.replace(/^[-*]\s+/,''))+'</li>');continue}
  closeList();para.push(line);
 }
 closePara();closeList();return result.join('');
};

